What this means in practice
---------------------------

You may read, run, modify, and redistribute this work for research, teaching,
personal, and other noncommercial purposes, provided you give attribution to
the author and to the companion manuscript relevant to the part you used
(see CITATION.cff).

You may not use this work, or anything derived from it, for commercial
purposes without a separate written licence. See "Commercial use" below.


How attribution travels
-----------------------

No one can grant rights they do not themselves hold. If someone builds this
work into something larger, they must attribute the author; and anyone using
*their* result still needs a licence for the part that originated here, so the
attribution and noncommercial conditions reach downstream on their own.

Deliberately absent: ShareAlike. It would force any derivative to carry this
same licence, which is a compatibility burden on anyone integrating this work
into a larger design — and it buys no additional protection, because
attribution and the noncommercial term already travel with the material.
What a derivative work chooses to call itself is not something this project
needs to control.


Commercial use
--------------

Commercial use is not granted by the public licence. That is not a closed
door — it is an open one with a doorbell, and the doorbell is answered.

If you want to use any part of this in a product, a funded evaluation, or an
industrial research programme, write to sigmansslee@gmail.com. Say which parts
interest you and what you intend to build. Terms are negotiable and I am the
sole copyright holder, so I can grant them directly — there is no institutional
approval chain in the way. Enquiries get a reply.


What a licence cannot do
------------------------

A licence governs copying and adaptation. It cannot compel citation, and it
cannot reach through a citation chain: if a third party cites a paper that
cited this work, that third party is under no licensing obligation here.
Attribution beyond direct reuse is an academic norm, enforced by convention
and journal policy rather than by copyright.


Setup note
----------

The two full licence texts are not reproduced here. Add them verbatim from the
canonical sources above into LICENSES/ — do not retype them, download them, so
that the operative text is exactly the official one. GitHub will then display
the licence correctly in the repository sidebar.
